  "body": "**Link to problem area**:\r\n* https://spec.matrix.org/v1.3/rooms/v1/\r\n* https://spec.matrix.org/v1.3/rooms/v2/\r\n\r\n* (it's not on https://spec.matrix.org/v1.3/rooms/ either)\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://spec.matrix.org/v1.3/appendices/#room-ids-and-event-ids says:\r\n\r\n> The format of an event ID depends upon the room version specification.\r\n\r\nand links to the above pages. However none of those pages appear to tell you the grammar for v1.\r\n\r\n**Issue**\r\n\r\nIt's unclear what the grammar for event IDs is; e.g. do they need to have a colon-separated domain name in?\r\n\r\nThe rule for redactions:\r\n\r\n> If the domain of the event_id of the event being redacted is the same as the domain of the event_id of the [m.room](http://m.room/).redaction, allow.\r\n\r\nsuggests that they must do.\r\n\r\nFurther, Synapse won't accept a V1/V2 event without a domain and it enforces that the domain is one that has a signature on the event.\r\n",
